[[File:Asofiko building.jpg|left|thumb|300x300px|The [[Asofiko]] ([[W:Legislature|legislature]]) building in the [[Òye]] commune]]
The [[Basic Law of Sanyan]] establishes the state as a {{W|Unitary state|unitary}} {{W|assembly-independent}} [[w:Directorial system|directorial republic]] that guarantees free access to the internet, {{W|freedom of the press}}, {{W|freedom of assembly}}, and {{W|reproductive rights}}. Several articles protecting the democratic nature of the state, including support for {{W|self-determination}} and {{W|social economic ownership}} are established within the document. Sanyan has been criticized by {{W|Western world|Western}} and capitalist nations as an {{W|authoritarianism|illiberal}} {{W|dominant party state|dominant party regime}}. Since the [[1960 Sanyan general election|1960 general election]], the [[Alaafia Party]] has maintained a {{W|supermajority}} in the ''[[Asofiko]]''. Although proponents of the ideology have avoided the "left/right" label, socialist academics have described Sanyan as being in line with {{W|African socialism|Kaftian socialism}}.

The Premier of Sanyan is selected by the delegates of the Asofiko rather than directly elected. Although {{W|universal suffrage}} for the Oloye and Asofiko elections are defined goals of the Basic Law, the Oloye is indirectly elected. The Oloye is elected by the membership of the [[Tribal Council]], which consists of representatives of Sanyan's x tribes. 

Ethnic minorities (such as [[Sanyan Creole people|Creoles]], [[Dakari diaspora|Dakari]] or [[Imfezzans]]) have increasingly gained representation in government since the [[Sanyan Emergency]], which saw the abolition of tribal based discrimination in housing, education, and employment in the post-Great Adonian War period. Prior to the social upheaval of the the emergency period, the country maintained the {{W|social caste}} system that it had developed in the early 19th century, which restricted citizenship based on {{W|jus sanguinis}} ("tribal heritage"). It had earlier emancipated and integrated repatriated Araucarians and their descendants, granting them rights to communal land and the potential for climbing the social ladder, while also denying Kaftians from the mainland and their descendants the same opportunities and rights. 
===Foreign relations===
[[File:Ayodeji Akinsanya.png|left|thumb|300x300px|[[Ayodeji Akinsanya]], the Sanyanian ambassador to the [[Adonian Community]]]]
Sanyan's foreign relations are handled by the [[Secretariat of Foreign Affairs (Sanyan)|Secretariat of Foreign Affairs]], which has its headquarters in [[tba]]. The first diplomatic relations were established on 10 March 1793 with the [[Kafto-Ethiopian Charter]], resulting in official diplomatic recognition between itself and the [[Maroon Confederacy]]. As of 1 April 2023, there are ??? diplomatic missions in Sanyan (to include trade/cultural offices, consulates, and embassies), while Sanyan has ??? missions abroad. 

Stemming from it's earlier history of {{W|Opposition to Atlantic slave trade|disrupting slavery}}, resistance to the [[colonization of Kaftia]], the post-decolonization years and the [[Kaftian Split]], Sanyan has strived to maintain solidarity with other people of the continent. Prior to the [[Bight of Ayorin Crisis]] the country maintained a strict {{W|international neutrality|neutral position}} regarding armed conflict. The country has maintained a balanced foreign policy based on adoption of dialogue, respect of international conventions, and non-interference of other country's internal affairs.Sanyan also supports the settlement of disputes by peaceful means, but has fully adopted a stance of legitimate {{W|self defense}}. Throughout the Kaftian Split, Sanyan served as a {{W|protecting power}} between several Kaftian nations, and later becoming a leading voice among the non-aligned Kaftian nations that were directly or indirectly destabilized by the superpower competition.  

Sanyan's foreign policy is mostly directed towards social development, de-militarization and cooperation within the Kaftian continent, especially in [[Sudanese Kaftia]]. Since the decolonization of Kaftia in the post-Great Adonian War years, it has maintained friendly relations with most Kaftia nations, with the exception of [[Wolffrea]]. In the modern era, Sanyan has directly fought in only one armed conflict; the [[Bight of Ayorin Crisis]], in which it was attacked by [[Ayorin]], marking the height of tensions between the two countries dating back to Sanyan's humanitarian and material support for the separatist [[State of Kokoro]] during the [[Ayori Civil War]]. Sanyan is a minor contributor to international peacekeeping and humanitarian efforts (mostly in [[Central Kaftia|Central]] and [[Northern Kaftia]]).
===Military===
{{Main|Sanyan Defense Force}}

{{See also|Mutual Arms and Technology Agreement}}
The main focus of the Defense Force is the protection of Sanyan's {{W|maritime borders}}, airspace, sovereignty and citizens. Sanyan has maintained conscription since the 1976 [[Bight of Ayorin Crisis]]. All citizens above age 18 are constitutionally required to serve in the military, usually at least 12 months, with exceptions being those currently enrolled in a institution of higher education, or those with severe disability. Top government officials have insisted for decades that conscription is invaluable to the maintenance of Sanyan's international neutrality and security, but some question the need for conscription in 21st century Sanyan. Critics have claim that external threats to Sanyan are negligible in this day and age (especially in regards to relations with [[Ayorin]] and [[Tamazgha]]) pointing to the existence of the [[Kaftian Union]] and the [[Adonian Community]] as enforcers of Sanyan's neutrality. Supporters argue that political instability in Central and North Kaftia necessitate a strong deterrent force.

The Sanyanian military consists of the [[Iyika]] (land defense) and the [[Coast Guard (Sanyan)|Coast Guard]] (maritime defense). Prior to the Bight of Ayorin crisis, Sanyan specifically avoided joining organizations that may have entailed a military alliance or signify an abandonment of neutrality. Presently, Sanyan is not a member of the [[KAFTIAN ALLIANCE]], and is absent from all other military and security organs of the [[Kaftian Union]].

Sanyan's history of foreign incursions, threats and unsolved disputes with Ayorin has lead Sanyan to develop a sizable, modern defense-oriented armed forces. Following the oil boom, underwent significant modernization and structural reform to shift their focus to a purely defensive posture. As of 2023, Sanyan has the world's ?? largest number of active troops (50,000), the world's ?? largest number of reserve troops (100,000), and the ?? largest defense budget ($1.08 billion). The Sanyan Defense Forces depend on a large variety of equipment produced by foreign manufactures.

