=== Immigration ===
{{Main|Immigration to Sanyan}}
Sanyan is an attractive destination especially in the region as it is a country with a strong currency that offers high living standards, including in education, work, wages and safety as well as an overall far higher [[W:Quality of life|quality of life]] compared to its neighbors. [[W:High-net-worth individual|High-net-worth]] or skilled immigrants worldwide are also attracted to Sanyan's low [[W:Tax rates|tax rates]] (e.g. no [[W:Income tax|income tax]]) and [[W:Ease of doing business|ease of doing business]]. The demographic background of these migrant groups is very diverse, with many of the countries of origin belonging to nations throughout Central and [[Northern Kaftia]]. A significant portion of them have qualified as [[W:Refugee|refugees]] since decolonization of the continent, and increasingly since the 1990s.[[File:Maroon island.png|thumb|[[Maroon Island]] ({{Langx|kzi|ⴻⵔⴻⴽⵢⵛⵢ ⵗⵎⵉⵏⵉⵔⴰ|Èrèkùṣù Òminira}}) in western Sanyan, home to the earliest settlement of repatriated [[Maroon Wars|Maroons]]|left]]

Immigration has historically been the main impetus for population growth in the country since the adoption of the [[Kafto-Ethiopian Charter]] in the late 18th century and subsequent close ties with [[Balisca]]. During the 19th to 20th centuries, Sanyan developed into a thriving and major [[W:Entrepôt|entrepôt]] as immigrants and merchants from all over south-central Kaftia were attracted by its [[W:Free economic zone|free trade policy]] and it's relatively liberal society free from colonial and imperialist influences. For a long period after its founding, the majority of Sanyan's population were immigrants (to include repatriated Kaftians). These people and their descendants also form the bulk of the modern Sanyanian population. 

After the [[Sanyan Emergency]], immigration laws were loosened as the city-state adopted a more cosmopolitan identity. This time, the initial strict controls on immigrant workers were relaxed as demand for [[W:Labour (economics)|labour]] grew with accelerating [[W:Industrialisation|industrialisation]]. Immigration would again become the largest contributor to population increase in Sanyan in the late 20th century and early 21st century. These recent immigration and immigrant workers in Sanyan have been closely associated with [[Economy of Sanyan|Sanyan's further economic]] [[W:Economic development|development]]. In 2018, the government introduced a [[W:Points-based immigration system|points-based immigration system]] for skilled applicants who wish to work in Sanyan.

